Title: Configuration
Content:
This page details Configuration. Basics The runtime entry point is io.yupiik.fusion.framework.api.configuration.Configuration, an injectable bean with a single operation: Optional<String> get(String key);
 A typical way to use it is to declare a configuration model - a record marked with @RootConfiguration - and inject the generated instance directly: @RootConfiguration("server")
public record ServerConfiguration(int port, String accessLogPattern) {}
 This reads server.port, server.accessLogPattern (or their environment variables SERVER_PORT, SERVER_ACCESSLOGPATTERN) at injection time. See the configuration model example for @Property, List, Map and nested models.

